From 4ed98c57948bc82d5741296ae8d0e009c97e4402 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Siddhartha Srivastava <siddhartha@delphai.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 16:10:59 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Stages are committed by their outputs; full traces only in
 disputes (build step 7)

TRACE_COMMIT's per-stage roots are now StageOutputRoot over the stage's T output rows (the
last layer's R2 rows). A disputed stage's trace is committed in a new top round as
nodeHash(BodyRoot, OutputRoot) (body = every other leaf, program order), with the output root
required to equal the committed one; play then bisects the body tree if the bodies differ, else
the output tree. One-step inputs are proven in the provider's body tree; stage inputs (one-step
and DATA_SERVE) against the previous stage's output root. BuildOneStep takes the previous
stage's outputs instead of its trace; uwcctl onestep reads prev_outputs; getjob reports the tree.

Full-trace commitments cost ~25x the GEMMs they describe; with output commitments the provider
computes only the forward pass (0.02 s vs 1.1 s per sequence-stage) and live lambda rises from
1.6e-4 to 0.03. Fault suite: every deviation that changes an output is caught by one
recomputation (50 of 60 random ones; the other 10 are absorbed by int8 quantization and rightly
settle). TestAgentTraceCommit checks the agent's split against TraceCommit.

